[{"id":"VRCE-2-16-1","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":1,"english":"Rāma saw his father, seated on a beautiful sofa with Kaikeyi, looking sorry and poorly and with his countenance dried up.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.698,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-18-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016001","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"da0b5407158ea4d871109302bafab9233d37e145566c10beb24cd3b31c466e7b","compact":"e367345ab329559b4da0572a6824e40f985c5361d8dc4385be31c2ff89912661","nasal":"31ba1b639ac949ba5c033a82c3d7238dedf09992665958958c7b405628118162"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-2","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":2,"english":"And humbly bowing down at the feet of his father first, he saluted Kaikeyi with due solemnity.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-18-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016002","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4aed2333dbc95ac8b15fbb4637a14f3bffd613ee1978b6005c870ed8e67a60d7","compact":"68d247246f452bfdd7602c8de0b259509a2962c948779b75ab31fb6d1b36e0af","nasal":"c3c33a1734bbdb7ff08a78f0cafd754fbe5976ed166d7accc27726df1901b8c1"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-3","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":3,"english":"Uttering the word \"Rāma\" only, the poor king with his eyes full of tears could not see him nor could he speak to him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.881,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-18-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016003","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3071dd055c9bd25ef12b52e805e77f4b7a79fa9d04256e6c64769d140f7795f0","compact":"8729db95afee1ec5ca968a74c5a4f3846d5ef8aeeb1c623a120a7da0b246c8ec","nasal":"8729db95afee1ec5ca968a74c5a4f3846d5ef8aeeb1c623a120a7da0b246c8ec"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-4","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":4,"english":"Seeing this unforeseen and terrible appearance of the king, like to a serpent trampled under foot, Rāma was exceedingly terrified.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.857,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-18-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016004","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8215301b262585460479d3b4dcddcca28d29316db2f87f319d734952d18528b0","compact":"f3181e20dca4b327aa2a64c064843e9049c43164d7a42226914761eaf1bf8d86","nasal":"97c68e7a3b0519d4e23a6f999dfe6cc0a77b31c5d5b85c07a1388890d3b54ecc"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-5","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":5,"english":"He was dejected and pulled down much with sorrow and penitence. He was sighing hot and hard and his heart was greatly pained. His heart was troubled like the wavy ocean agitating though incapable of agitation, and clouded like the Sun possessed by Rahu, and (that of) an ascetic speaking falsehood.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-18-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016005","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ac014ae505e7d909b509377b673e896c4b80954df8514f278f55d9b59a7ef799","compact":"55f42a386286a10ad5522308d31d21463f07958e514005df11cc305bc50f8613","nasal":"f17528acbb5bdf2c6902c02fade1e227cc3d605a7dc9c17017352359b4b6e4f1"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-6","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":6,"english":"He was dejected and pulled down much with sorrow and penitence. He was sighing hot and hard and his heart was greatly pained. His heart was troubled like the wavy ocean agitating though incapable of agitation, and clouded like the Sun possessed by Rahu, and (that of) an ascetic speaking falsehood.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.938,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-18-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016006","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ec0abd2b6e82190b81d5a797b346c08eb4a2e30f606a17697c66ce775e18bf4e","compact":"d53e80270f8971b48d5fe32c018d20b2e26c12b4b0e1167445a9136656b90bad","nasal":"a83a0070b0c9a43176cc540c9ecf159a6b5cc4fdd511a33e220bb48b4a958f85"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-7","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":7,"english":"Thinking of this unthought of sorrow of the king he became agitated like to the ocean during the course of the full-moon.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.764,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-18-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016007","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"60b4ba52b8648035062506d4b0fb2f913531465b8027ed1d8765021aafab1206","compact":"8df22ad31d1d9b5bff1db9da421be90af34a0379a3909ecedb8de9d7c966b32a","nasal":"6c79c1e74d0883bf6fba4671bbe6fac81de1c3c8dad0c85be6d68b0d143bf67b"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-8","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":8,"english":"And clever Rāma, intent on his father's welfare, thought within himself:, Why does not the king display joy on my arrival to-day.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.85,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-18-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016008","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7040213eade00811fc18dc2cec3b5b788edc46cfa8896509d1ebf7694aa95aee","compact":"b7936eda5286b437f3b74be316bc39a9bb6705b2f197d7bd221a265ab7a4e12d","nasal":"7b6d06958f4d89b9b62a8325fe23f572799bf0f4343ed37ca208e5fd794fdbe2"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-9","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":9,"english":"Angry though, he used to express joy whenever he saw me; then why does his sorrow prevail even seeing me to-day?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.882,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-18-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016009","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3c746b6ab36757c81881632b78313dc67c0ff4eff8325534a91a2ba4d61ee19f","compact":"553239a0cd1418fd109d47e003a8ba7468945f166ce8b031b1b072f3055e5ae3","nasal":"553239a0cd1418fd109d47e003a8ba7468945f166ce8b031b1b072f3055e5ae3"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-10","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":10,"english":"Being pressed with sorrow, Rāma of pale countenance, like one miserable, saluting KaikeyI, spoke to her the following words.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.796,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-18-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016010","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"65df33f7eea4ed1be8af8808baa4abb77e09dbfcdf381becbf182607e4a25b19","compact":"ba0fde50a984e15b07d861df2b32257d46d11c4ada73e010d9a9ae6a0423a318","nasal":"7eab4f9cec5329ed9395ca27f930e6eebdab8511f861e74cce136c07e04eeaf4"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-11","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":11,"english":"Is it not that I committed some offence through ignorance that I see my father angry? Do you propitiate him therefore.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.846,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-18-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016011","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"22a34bc8a7e15b347ffb9561644b8d7c91ed8512ccc7f2cc71f60f2a4ed4e286","compact":"aa15ee922da675bfbacf2bbf128ffbaf5f316d4520d53a634764123c6662d29c","nasal":"aa15ee922da675bfbacf2bbf128ffbaf5f316d4520d53a634764123c6662d29c"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-12","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":12,"english":"Is he subject to any physical or mental disturbance? Oh! happiness uninterrupted is very dear.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.675,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-18-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016012","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"53f51c90e3f71a3054891edb704e07a21b6b7d11da09a73ed160477e32557875","compact":"afe61257aa27cb4243a184479906daf60f364d41f4647cd4aa8aa91d52f271c4","nasal":"afe61257aa27cb4243a184479906daf60f364d41f4647cd4aa8aa91d52f271c4"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-13","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":13,"english":"Has any evil befallen the good-looking Bharata or high-souled Śatrughna? Is it not all well with my mothers.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.672,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-18-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016013","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c1921c5747ccde7af912fdac75bd7c10c292e09fc85b6181fc01d86a6e805887","compact":"ab107c6ed66b8e432509f1d3a3f812fe117249782b7be1e6836c8b341b44c9f2","nasal":"0313ad56198d0884280739fdf6fa9acc948c45ba9eddc6f866a1c5d3194d4ec3"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-14","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":14,"english":"Dissatisfying the king, disregarding his words and offending him, I do not want to breathe for a single moment.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-18-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016014","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b847ea162324c8ac198798022ee253c88b5470cb475c1cee0a92417e15de84f7","compact":"8da789ecb8d77be93fb89413adfde094f2f00a618b38f4b299ce21b6fa0d692f","nasal":"8da789ecb8d77be93fb89413adfde094f2f00a618b38f4b299ce21b6fa0d692f"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-15","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":15,"english":"How can a man disregard him who is god himself seen and felt, and who is looked upon as a cause from whom he has sprung.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-18-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016015","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"915d8a542ede70426d0768c48c0e1e36d8d0239853a5e8d231bd5ea272b91454","compact":"680e0fe7a7a3a599d515787534287474224ca8773aa4c1f316a4c90874d42f13","nasal":"00e0303401a43eb2cddfeb1f7debaca85d5db5514a268cf3a72c730e9d717d34"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-16","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":16,"english":"Oh mother, have you spoken any harsh word to my father either through anger or through haughtiness for which his mind is thus pulled down?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.733,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-18-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016016","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f7698aa6946f88e5dbac8b7e7100d5e53a15c8cff29b7c908acb3c263105e224","compact":"8058e8bb41fface817d38ee113949222f4144548417843dbbfe94748232116a3","nasal":"8058e8bb41fface817d38ee113949222f4144548417843dbbfe94748232116a3"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-17","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":17,"english":"Oh worshipful one, tell me all this, who am exceedingly anxious to get at the real truth. Why has this unforeseen sorrow overtaken the heart of the lord of men?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-18-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016017","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a874172e03e8309268aa1a3b51bbce33c82d2c48f34d6223e4df928a46fc0d72","compact":"874d640bed8ba1c1e192b4c669c36acd9a11c64d8bd52585dfe8e8c142b2ac98","nasal":"874d640bed8ba1c1e192b4c669c36acd9a11c64d8bd52585dfe8e8c142b2ac98"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-18","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":18,"english":"Oh! shame to me. May it not please you, Oh worshipful lady, to speak such words to me. I can at the king's words jump into the fire. Being ordered by him, who is my father and who is my king especially, I can drink virulent poison and drown into the ocean. Speak you, Oh worshipful lady, what is the desire of the king, and know that I shall carry it out, Rāma does not contradict what he has once spoken.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.878,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-18-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016018","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"079d3be3011fc1e07076f1d98f5e0c0cdd40838f3dc5413203d4a8c80b79e7a9","compact":"3d2eb6a4bdcd1a77cc7242a4db3c7728a25cf645edac6a43da30d2fc65c16fca","nasal":"3d2eb6a4bdcd1a77cc7242a4db3c7728a25cf645edac6a43da30d2fc65c16fca"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-19","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":19,"english":"Oh! shame to me. May it not please you, Oh worshipful lady, to speak such words to me. I can at the king's words jump into the fire. Being ordered by him, who is my father and who is my king especially, I can drink virulent poison and drown into the ocean. Speak you, Oh worshipful lady, what is the desire of the king, and know that I shall carry it out, Rāma does not contradict what he has once spoken.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.821,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-18-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016019","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1f173fa4f52e9faba016cb69b42100b6a6ed500480cda68514b9f2d9127e1449","compact":"204ab501e8cb68a5808062fbcd1ba05250dd7bf222604d29a149e2c5aa1f442f","nasal":"3619245710326dc7ac449ce081a65b07ee6cb6a53db62411fbd7eb6571760c0e"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-20","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":20,"english":"Then that wicked Kaikeyi spoke these highly cruel words to Rāma, simple and truthful.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-18-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016020","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a7e5839d86d258471f6e06ccf4dd7c3d837229bb1f8798865ae84ea2bef9fbce","compact":"5b85b247b18f3999ae39104e07342302aef5d9bfa14f9dfd918ad9a5f74c5e55","nasal":"5b85b247b18f3999ae39104e07342302aef5d9bfa14f9dfd918ad9a5f74c5e55"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-21","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":21,"english":"Foremerly in a great war between the gods and Asuras, your father, being wounded with shafts was tended by me for which he conferred upon me two boons.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-18-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016021","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3d57e7c197899f8e8dcce8f62a5f1a95ea096a31febd76338afb87cd91328c22","compact":"5c73b1c1899573b10db3b3cd0e75a5a42085da80982887cf63865b8ef8aa5f55","nasal":"5c73b1c1899573b10db3b3cd0e75a5a42085da80982887cf63865b8ef8aa5f55"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-22","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":22,"english":"Of these two boons I have asked of the king the installation of Bharata, and the departure of Rāghava into the Dandaka forest even this very day.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-18-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016022","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"04640960974fe8b76687f6c23d42e83623fa47e9356baf66094e76bac91da93c","compact":"6f7d3886ff9b6d588d963fc9ef38891df8ec7d85471e35e05eb53f55150ea936","nasal":"ca1c17fb318bbdcc7a99046bff1fb8085a5dbd9dad737ac00f35b05a9c09f058"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-23","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":23,"english":"Oh you best among men, if do you wish to keep your father's vows as well as yours, hear what I say.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.883,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-18-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016023","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"02910151e8b4f913ebe4b2906f3ae941a0d3a1179d2f11a3d65f8e6059cd15bc","compact":"68a983f6ea1d6a576ed32b3d7b16877c459d0656f976ce2cfc3205c0acad23f3","nasal":"68a983f6ea1d6a576ed32b3d7b16877c459d0656f976ce2cfc3205c0acad23f3"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-24","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":24,"english":"Your father is bound to me by promise, obeying therefore your father's mandate, do you repair to the forest for nine years and five.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.862,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-18-31"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016024","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3c9b88b8705e211869709db4cbb8eda465ca1e2eb36bce5fc9615e16f5bbc085","compact":"61b4bcc446327cb080ffb3f305cc8f8af507d9f67c35e8d602ca6b210c518642","nasal":"9465728368fffa2c523b5d57ceb536a6eb8ad4217487a2d11b46fd9dc712cb7c"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-25","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":25,"english":"Forsaking this installation, do you repair to Dandaka forest for seven and seven years and wear bark and matted hair.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.825,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-18-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016025","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b90122d79f7409dfbae015202dde91b4c1ffe5d5e80e757214cff288922a80d0","compact":"785f1bbf280ac5117bc0e4612f6a1aed84a0ea29102a74b145e9b313f5657137","nasal":"1ee502fea84b04a7454870df6ad1cda963e88b5e6d60ad819ef63fbeacf690f8"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-26","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":26,"english":"And here in this Kosala let Bharata govern the world, adorned with many pearls and diamonds, with elephants, horses and chariots.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.678,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-18-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016026","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"153540490008e3781723bc9dfe205da975b1dc0e0d5c033935497a63a61bb4d0","compact":"8c6e461da7d8a73200cf0d5378ee8e4e64d6a346bd941e4114c4e0a88cef7535","nasal":"0882532ee0cc9e614090c965f5f59d17d158fb7cca30f3a05225061596c223c4"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-27","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":27,"english":"Hearing these unpleasant words like to death, Rama, the destroyer of foes, was not pained, and spoke thus to Kaikeyī.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-19-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016027","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6bfbddfd257a18887e557d7ef295e04af1808f85635bb387467fde5df7b1044e","compact":"5bbe1aac764734cdc01d4c843c9131fa9512bfd164f34ced6f709484135e6878","nasal":"5bbe1aac764734cdc01d4c843c9131fa9512bfd164f34ced6f709484135e6878"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-28","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":28,"english":"Be it what you say; carrying out the promise of the king, I shall repair to the forest from this place wearing bark and matted hair.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-19-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016028","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f722d3ecdad038808a5c1884131830357b9daddb945cc70900ba91e588b730b4","compact":"79cca485b58e9b36a6645a1264365bc63173df6df9ab18a972a9306a1da04eb5","nasal":"79cca485b58e9b36a6645a1264365bc63173df6df9ab18a972a9306a1da04eb5"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-29","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":29,"english":"Now I want to know only why that lord of the earth, invincible and the conqueror of foes, does not receive me in the same way as he used to do on previous occasions.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.852,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-19-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016029","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"09086b7fb00a8e820b279cfd323aec3b2731dcac0d6f0e19d5a9f914719996e0","compact":"5a1b1f62f45a004041f70bc42d32eab1ffaa799be2888bf54caa9562e8cf530a","nasal":"c1bb17771c82f39e784b4e0fdb91e26b51b503c5685e0961e62e61fa7bc1ea6f"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-30","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":30,"english":"be not angry, Oh worshipful one, I speak before you, be you propitiated well, and I shall go to the forest wearing bark and matted hair.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.869,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-19-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016030","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4ccfc8e12919c499b51217c223da7a6a7c0c04dfc851f9ea0e148099767009ff","compact":"ee9d3621b78cf1583f3cbdd2ce0db3bea6ccd0957c007a7e82707f70b2673c84","nasal":"ee9d3621b78cf1583f3cbdd2ce0db3bea6ccd0957c007a7e82707f70b2673c84"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-31","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":31,"english":"What is there that I cannot perform, considering it good without suspicion, if I am ordered so by my well-wisher, spiritual leader, father and king, who acknowledges your service (rendered in time of danger).* *The epithet Krtajñena may as well as be rendered into general terms; such as 'who acknowledges services rendered to him.' Here in translation I have followed the commentator who has restricted it to the special sense suitable to the occasion.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.656,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-19-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016031","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cd7040d8cf1010d99e103a6503f7adc1cd90f57f4512aecc4a03546edede748b","compact":"610deb964ca69fb2722b4b6cd20d79d197bd77f5a17236e3c17f4c68eca7af1b","nasal":"610deb964ca69fb2722b4b6cd20d79d197bd77f5a17236e3c17f4c68eca7af1b"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-32","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":32,"english":"But this one sorrow burns my heart, why king did not tell me personally of the installation of Bharata.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.796,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-19-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016032","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1e511b5b3bc70c2b55fda607f7503448d10c09104f84e6fa2ac434bd44daf18a","compact":"4016dbc9fcbe5f3a24312a8ec611f3077f7fc339b765ed79ab00af58a778d593","nasal":"44ff34c961730bc0941dfcb0c3ec7df942145c828d69e8724845db7d0b537a40"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-33","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":33,"english":"What of the command of the king, my father, I shall even at your mandate joyfully make over to Bharata, my kingdom, Sītā, wealth and even my life, thereby satisfying you, and fulfilling my promise.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.929,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-19-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016033","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"90e6a68e57fc13f29c634aa7247bce43d8fb954e8ca0d3b30e5bf2904e58ea91","compact":"754491a042ed0dadd47a79208c56e1240a7865af13723dd66cec93048d535f23","nasal":"e8049892163cb46b72a8896e5745df2d8921dbbc2a7dfb5db4c4f7eec0ec6ff6"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-34","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":34,"english":"What of the command of the king, my father, I shall even at your mandate joyfully make over to Bharata, my kingdom, Sītā, wealth and even my life, thereby satisfying you, and fulfilling my promise.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-19-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016034","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"764b0bfdbf85a24076d5d497e34736a8375d276cab7a0489bc8659c9ba81c904","compact":"2c26f0003b3014e40c8bb4198f4820e35f87f243f708a973f7604bb24fc11cf3","nasal":"d1c3181a5e0d93612d5a6ae21873239ea689c8e1443196b45b2e4b6ca4f156f7"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-35","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":35,"english":"Do you now console the bashful king; why has he, with his eyes steadily fixed on the ground, been shedding tears slowly?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.667,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-19-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016035","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"61f20a7e75b1f77978a6e2596dc4780b0734e79dd20056a512bc9705faa5d2b2","compact":"c7f7bc778693c29373bcfbb91944de252ddb850af8e8dce4ac66d8770a50666f","nasal":"745e05a310232ea3de9861bfdac7a111769182073feac674a013823974d5dcca"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-36","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":36,"english":"Let messengers, with fast going steeds go today at the command of the king to fetch Bharata from his maternal uncle's house.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-19-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016036","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"14a9e0f2684736adb77da2b96925bb75e7c369133cd2f81f9b3a3f1d8f98a4b4","compact":"6f3d9fc9cf720f982226da55934e8d882c9134450a4b17d26feaeb68e1943f60","nasal":"7831d432dac4d19b4c462453921838c663f7bac74f343b1e5ea9aa7855ce236b"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-37","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":37,"english":"I shall, not even judging the propriety of my father's words, speedily repair to the forest of Dandaka for fourteen years.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.721,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-19-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016037","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c1486667f561667fedac4911b4adf045783c2fcc3e93a18f380ebf07994d6e0a","compact":"4b3d68a2ddd75987c0c2e6cf887a9798b4faa197144fad9e65edfdc9f3a9951e","nasal":"b5d32dadde579f57609d686992b4bdb8c8a7cc0523f5f7bbdb1884ce6466e784"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-38","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":38,"english":"Hearing those words of Rāma, Kaikeyi was pleased, and being certain about his departure, hurried on Raghava.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.87,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-19-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016038","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bbf02add1f61966f2f4b0a8a8ceffede98badda6312b00a82c68a077f5ee31f4","compact":"148f36b0da4e6152ab936683f4fff1ae6fd52beded516aab028943007656ad9e","nasal":"148f36b0da4e6152ab936683f4fff1ae6fd52beded516aab028943007656ad9e"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-39","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":39,"english":"Let it be that messengers with fast going steeds shall go to bring Bharata from his maternal uncle's residence.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.603,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-19-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016039","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"15ecc26d941d3d6d2608d3eb96684d6a76e7a0b291c61707ba0fdc5f55f9389e","compact":"15285e34580bffc5a6ffe9e74527d134093cc00c84f1d3e3aeb48033bae4d5a7","nasal":"172c4d0f136353abc3729735b9a2420694fae0c70603d5f67381e948928dd897"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-40","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":40,"english":"I do not think it proper for you, O Rāma, to delay, when you are so anxious; it behoves you therefore to depart from this place speedily to the forest.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-19-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016040","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3d6d7df8abe7a9ac4c723b19c4505988f442953ff28f219db244da695ff076a0","compact":"a78eb502f286e8ce6d20da579cc9bb7dd8ebcf57faba3de3729b2ab2249cb055","nasal":"19c337344fbac0e1e00de479a4ffcab84e06d8a4f7f3b775127ef47d11bca73f"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-41","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":41,"english":"The king being abashed, does not himself address you, there is nothing else than this. Do you, Oh best of men, dispel this wretchedness of his.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-19-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016041","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3f3a6dc379293c619d0835229fcfc3f1af79dc2812cde2c814d34db9c6e225a8","compact":"2f589d27b6d7af8be300fe479422c4b972d5b7e0020b63b663d99d089a99e757","nasal":"659b068892813dc9f8227aaf9c23a1676932f0831f46b83ea925b7f14a3b666e"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-42","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":42,"english":"As long as you shall not hurriedly depart from his presence, Oh Rāma, your father shall not bathe, or eat anything.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.785,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-19-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016042","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2547f41e8a752bfadebb7270631fb7d9f8808ad551aded23f60b9f6bc67205c1","compact":"02801b2d7f196d21194afa979fc68cab5f4d00721c29a57dfe1b20362b7a9e9f","nasal":"869fccff00457b0b553e55a7fdcc76e4c76f0f1cb65cabf20042a48acb99e57b"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-43","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":43,"english":"'Oh fie!' 'what affliction' sobbing hard with these words, the monarch, filled with sorrow, swooned away and fell down upon the sofa, embellished with gold.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.913,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-19-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016043","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ee2b781ff5f55f7629ee61b92997efd5fc83ba7de77e1c3c4d5176801b8ac47f","compact":"05f4373fe53f6462407441dda22dc0a10d7eae26eecc1bc9bdf77c40bd365098","nasal":"f2839216278c48fd9504709eaa074b062dd3e74883bd649f280bc1fa72e3c6da"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-44","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":44,"english":"Raising the king up, Rāma, being directed by Kaikeyī, began to hurry on his departure to the forest, like to a steed struck sharp with a whip.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.746,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-19-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016044","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"36b0d113c3dc5d67d1aee89d32ff35ba7804f36abfe149877f0bda9cdedc8a19","compact":"a2e33411bed89744a3a94e80003e12cb08079a7785c6504c99c8cced40d11b03","nasal":"4977bd87144548a52016b426534ff5fe501fadc396a25d9ca615971b772c83cb"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-45","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":45,"english":"Hearing those cruel and unpleasant words of the wicked Kaikeyi, Rama, not being distressed, began to address her with the following words.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.71,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-19-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016045","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d06a8e3fa6a841cf73c3a0d681d2141de83f720a4c32661f9ef9050f05b2655e","compact":"2086c63ba94551d14c3f85147d33dc2eaacf23ab253d8c7f4a84be3a0bcfe7a0","nasal":"2086c63ba94551d14c3f85147d33dc2eaacf23ab253d8c7f4a84be3a0bcfe7a0"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-46","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":46,"english":"Oh worshipful one, being addicted to wealth do I not long for living in this world; like to Rșis, know me, to be well established in pure religion.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.844,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-19-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016046","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a0a0acccb92f17e40d2872f6d3a0d6f0ff10a7a221cba5908e8ed8738acb9291","compact":"760d6fdeaae3f8ad61cad304fa2afd8a5f727af4240c2cced8a7c2da59a08375","nasal":"760d6fdeaae3f8ad61cad304fa2afd8a5f727af4240c2cced8a7c2da59a08375"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-16-47","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":16,"verse":47,"english":"If I can, even at the sacrifice of my own life, satisfy my worshipful father, rest assured it is to be done first in all manner.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.968,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-19-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2016047","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4331498aec7fe6f085301fa61f54c8d842a106577aac78688cd709d0b31